  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2904.01 Grant Conditions.\n\n(a) Grant funds awarded pursuant to the substance abuse enforcement program shall support activities for:\n\n(1) The investigation and apprehension of individuals or organizations that are involved in narcotic-related drug use and trafficking that is identified by:\n\na. Using statistics and information to place additional patrol and investigative presence at locations, times, and places where there has been a significant convergence of motor vehicle crashes, crimes, and illegal drug use; and\n\nb. Using statistics and information to place additional patrol and investigative presence in corridors known to be used by drug dealers for shipment of illegal drugs into the state;\n\n(2) Absent unanticipated staff shortages, relieving dedicated patrol units from taking calls for service;\n\n(3) Promoting multi-jurisdictional law enforcement collaboration and increased information sharing through the IAC; and\n\n(4) The reduction of narcotics sales, abuse, and deaths.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 2900) #11150, EXEMPT, eff 8-5-16; ss by #12227, EXEMPT, eff 6-29-17; ss by #12527, eff 5-11-18; ss by #12894, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 10-3-19, EXPIRED: 3-31-20\n\nNew. #13230, eff 7-9-21",
